[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Starlark for .NET - futures extension
VERSION: 0.1
OPTIONS:
  ENABLE_MID: True

[GRAMMAR]
ELEMENTS:
- TAG: REQUIREMENT
  FIELDS:
  - TITLE: UID
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: STATUS
    TYPE: SingleChoice(Draft, Active, Implemented, Open)
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: TITLE
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: STATEMENT
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: VERIFICATION
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  - TITLE: COMMENT
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False

[FREETEXT]
An opt-in extension that lets a script start work concurrently and collect the results. It is not part of the
Starlark specification and is off unless the host enables the dialect flag. Standard programs behave identically with
the flag off.
[/FREETEXT]

[SECTION]
TITLE: Prerequisite

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FUT-PRE-001
STATUS: Open
TITLE: Per-call execution context
STATEMENT: >>>
The interpreter shall keep all per-run mutable state (step counter, deadline, call depth, recursion set, string
element mode, memory budget) in an execution context created for each call, not in the Interpreter object, so that
a frozen module can be called from many threads at once.
<<<
COMMENT: This is also the fix for HOST-RUN-006.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FUT-PRE-002
STATUS: Open
TITLE: Thread-safe frozen modules
STATEMENT: >>>
Calling functions of a frozen module concurrently from many threads shall produce the same results as calling them
one at a time, shown by a stress test.
<<<

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: Language

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FUT-LANG-001
STATUS: Open
TITLE: Dialect flag
STATEMENT: >>>
The names spawn, all_of and first_of and the future type shall exist only when the dialect flag EnableFutures is set.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FUT-LANG-002
STATUS: Open
TITLE: Spawning
STATEMENT: >>>
spawn(function, *args, **kwargs) shall start the call on another thread and return a future immediately.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FUT-LANG-003
STATUS: Open
TITLE: Collecting a result
STATEMENT: >>>
future.get() shall block until the call finishes and return its result, or raise the error the call raised, with the
original source location. future.done() shall return a bool without blocking.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FUT-LANG-004
STATUS: Open
TITLE: Waiting on several futures
STATEMENT: >>>
all_of(futures) shall return the results as a list in the order of the argument. first_of(futures) shall return the
index and result of the first to finish and shall be documented as nondeterministic.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FUT-LANG-005
STATUS: Open
TITLE: Isolation
STATEMENT: >>>
Arguments shall be frozen when passed to spawn and the result frozen when it returns. A spawned function that mutates
a value it captured shall fail with the usual frozen-value error, so tasks cannot race on data.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FUT-LANG-006
STATUS: Open
TITLE: Determinism
STATEMENT: >>>
Apart from first_of, the observable result of a program shall not depend on thread scheduling.
<<<

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: Host integration

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FUT-HOST-001
STATUS: Open
TITLE: Host tasks as futures
STATEMENT: >>>
When futures are enabled, a registered host function that returns Task or Task of T shall return a future to the
script without blocking, so a script can start several host operations and then collect them.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FUT-HOST-002
STATUS: Open
TITLE: Limits and cancellation
STATEMENT: >>>
A spawned call shall inherit the step, time and memory limits and the cancellation token of its parent, cancelling the
parent shall cancel its tasks, and a future not collected by the end of the run shall be cancelled.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FUT-HOST-003
STATUS: Open
TITLE: Concurrency cap
STATEMENT: >>>
The host shall be able to cap the number of tasks running at once for a run.
<<<

[/SECTION]

[SECTION]
TITLE: Verification

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FUT-VER-001
STATUS: Open
TITLE: Equivalence property
STATEMENT: >>>
A property test shall show that, for generated programs, spawning a call and getting its result gives the same value
(or the same error) as calling it inline.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FUT-VER-002
STATUS: Open
TITLE: Checker support
STATEMENT: >>>
The static checker shall know the future type and the signatures of spawn, all_of and first_of when the flag is set.
<<<

[/SECTION]
